// SesiDo Summarize Tool
allow "../../build/index" in with SesiDo; set_alias("SesiDo-Lite", "gemini-3.1-flash-lite"); set_alias("SesiDo-Lite-Power", "gemini-3.5-flash-lite") ; let logTag = "[" + SesiDo.universalTime + "]"; print logTag + " [SUMMARIZE]"; SesiDo.summarize(args); print "[SUMMARIZE ENDED]"

/*

    Description:
        Summarizes a given text or document using Sesi's native summarization tool.

    Args:
        args: An object with the following key:
            text: (string, required) The text to summarize.
            file: (string, optional) The path to the file to summarize.

    Quality Guidelines:
        - Maintain a consistent summarization style (e.g., concise, factual).
        - Capture the main points of the text.
        - Ensure the summary is easy to understand.
        - Avoid generating overly long or detailed summaries.
        - Maintain a consistent summarization style (e.g., concise, factual).
        - Capture the main points of the text.
        - Ensure the summary is easy to understand.
        - Avoid generating overly long or detailed summaries.

    Output:
        - Generates a summary of the given text.
        - Saves the summary to the artifacts directory.
        - Returns a message indicating the location of the generated summary.

Examples:
        - npm run summarize "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The dog was sleeping peacefully."
        - npm run summarize file:///path/to/file.txt

*/